        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left medial calf symptoms (patient report)"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "For the past 7 days, mild symptoms in the left medial calf, described as a tender line over a previous varicose vein area. Earlier in the week there was some redness and slight warmth, and it felt like a bruise; it now seems to be settling. Described as a strip perhaps the length of a hand and not very wide. No whole-leg swelling. Able to weight bear and walk inside."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
